# Git LFS patterns for large binary files.
#
# GPU_RUNBOOK outputs under runs/gpu_* are explicitly allowed by .gitignore
# and use Git LFS for checkpoints and validation prediction arrays. Other
# historical checkpoints, caches and archives remain ignored.
#
# The parquet pattern is deliberately commented out.  The repository tracks two
# small (1.45 MB) test-set parquet files under test_features_with_entity/ that
# were uploaded through the GitHub web UI, i.e. stored as plain blobs.  With
# `filter=lfs` in force, git applies the LFS clean filter locally and computes a
# pointer hash that can never equal the stored plain-blob hash - the files then
# show up as permanently "modified", and any `git add` would silently rewrite
# them into LFS pointers.  They are far below GitHub's 100 MB limit, so plain
# blobs are the correct storage for them.
# *.parquet filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.npz     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pt      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.pth     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.zip     filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.7z      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
